    <string name="help_title">Supported firmware</string>
    <string name="help_text">• Android 2.3–4.4: 32-bit ARM firmware, runs through QEMU.\n• Android 5.0–17: arm64 firmware and GSIs, run natively on the phone.\n\nFormats:\n• CWM/TWRP recovery ZIP (MIUI, CyanogenMod, ports, most custom ROMs);\n• Samsung: Odin .tar / .tar.md5 or a ZIP with AP_*.tar.md5;\n• Google factory images (.tgz / .zip);\n• system.img (ext4, sparse), TWRP backup system.ext4.win;\n• OTA with system.new.dat(.br) + system.transfer.list.\n\nBest if the archive contains boot.img: the service start order is taken from it.</string>
    <string name="vs_screen">Guest screen</string>
    <string name="vs_fixed_2x">Android 2.x uses a fixed 480×800 screen at 240 dpi.</string>
    <string name="vs_screen_hint">A smaller screen makes the system faster.</string>
    <string name="vs_fbhz">Guest refresh, Hz</string>
    <string name="vs_fbhz_hint">Frame rate the emulated display asks the machine for. 60 is the default the engine is tuned for; 90–144 helps on high-refresh phones if the engine honors it — an unsupported engine just keeps 60. Reboot the VM after a change.</string>
    <string name="vs_perf">Performance</string>
    <string name="vs_gpu">Phone GPU</string>
